1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,759
Chai Corner has six people now,
but nobody knows who the boss is.

2
00:00:05,059 --> 00:00:06,805
Ravi tells Asha one thing.

3
00:00:06,805 --> 00:00:08,693
Kabir tells her the opposite.

4
00:00:09,243 --> 00:00:12,917
Two people wash the same cups,
and nobody counts the money.

5
00:00:13,217 --> 00:00:16,811
By evening, the cash box is
short, and the team is arguing.

6
00:00:17,461 --> 00:00:19,120
Good chai is not enough.

7
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:21,463
He needs rules for running the team.

8
00:00:22,163 --> 00:00:26,266
A hundred years ago, a French mining
engineer had the same problem.

9
00:00:26,566 --> 00:00:28,513
His name was Henri Fayol.

10
00:00:28,513 --> 00:00:31,800
He ran a big mining
company for thirty years.

11
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:36,547
In 1916, he wrote a book about
managing a whole company.

12
00:00:36,847 --> 00:00:39,853
Many call him the father
of modern management.

13
00:00:40,503 --> 00:00:42,931
So, what is administrative management?

14
00:00:43,231 --> 00:00:47,403
It is running the whole organization
from the top, with clear functions

15
00:00:47,403 --> 00:00:48,461
and principles.

16
00:00:48,811 --> 00:00:50,852
Taylor studied one worker's task.

17
00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:52,894
Fayol studied the whole company.

18
00:00:53,544 --> 00:00:56,964
First, Fayol said every
manager does five things.

19
00:00:57,414 --> 00:00:58,314
Planning.

20
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:01,336
Looking ahead, like buying
extra milk for the weekend.

21
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:02,586
Organizing.

22
00:01:02,516 --> 00:01:05,729
Arranging people and things,
like who works where.

23
00:01:06,079 --> 00:01:06,979
Commanding.

24
00:01:06,918 --> 00:01:09,162
Giving the team clear instructions.

25
00:01:09,512 --> 00:01:10,514
Coordinating.

26
00:01:10,514 --> 00:01:13,291
Making sure everyone's work fits together.

27
00:01:13,641 --> 00:01:14,727
And controlling.

28
00:01:14,727 --> 00:01:16,779
Checking that things go to plan.

29
00:01:17,429 --> 00:01:19,706
Next, he gave fourteen principles.

30
00:01:19,706 --> 00:01:22,303
A principle is a simple rule to follow.

31
00:01:22,653 --> 00:01:24,198
Here are all fourteen.

32
00:01:24,198 --> 00:01:26,550
Let's look closely at four big ones.

33
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,425
Division of work.

34
00:01:28,425 --> 00:01:31,929
Each person does one job,
and gets really good at it.

35
00:01:32,279 --> 00:01:36,372
Asha makes the tea, Kabir handles
money, and Meena cleans cups.

36
00:01:36,722 --> 00:01:38,062
Unity of command.

37
00:01:38,062 --> 00:01:41,131
Each worker takes orders
from only one boss.

38
00:01:41,481 --> 00:01:44,026
So Asha now listens only to Ravi.

39
00:01:44,026 --> 00:01:45,881
No more opposite orders.

40
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,230
Scalar chain.

41
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:51,217
Orders travel in one clear line,
from the top to the bottom.

42
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:53,281
But a long chain is slow.

43
00:01:53,281 --> 00:01:56,358
The stove helper needs
change from the cash helper.

44
00:01:56,708 --> 00:01:59,118
With Ravi's okay, they talk directly.

45
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:01,681
Fayol called this shortcut a gang plank.

46
00:02:02,031 --> 00:02:03,168
Esprit de corps.

47
00:02:03,168 --> 00:02:05,017
That's French for team spirit.

48
00:02:05,367 --> 00:02:09,796
Ravi praises the whole team together,
so everyone works for Chai Corner.

49
00:02:10,446 --> 00:02:11,375
Quick check.

50
00:02:11,375 --> 00:02:15,263
Two helpers at the same level
talk directly, with Ravi's okay.

51
00:02:15,263 --> 00:02:16,690
What is this called?

52
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:19,495
Gang plank!

53
00:02:19,495 --> 00:02:23,747
A shortcut between people at the
same level, with the boss's okay.

54
00:02:24,347 --> 00:02:25,356
So, remember.

55
00:02:25,656 --> 00:02:31,325
Fayol gave five functions: plan, organize,
command, coordinate, and control.

56
00:02:31,675 --> 00:02:34,935
He gave fourteen principles
for running the whole company.

57
00:02:35,285 --> 00:02:39,715
The key ones: division of work, unity
of command, scalar chain, and team

58
00:02:39,715 --> 00:02:40,615
spirit.

59
00:02:40,921 --> 00:02:45,060
Next time, we'll meet Max Weber,
and his idea of bureaucracy.
